# BaseNode Implementation Guide

## Core Architecture

The BaseNode system uses a **single source of truth** pattern where Zustand store holds the complete graph JSON, and ReactFlow renders it as a visual interface. Each node follows a strict contract to ensure consistency across the system.

### Data Flow
```
User Interaction → Node UI (ui.tsx) → Store Action (updateNodeConfig) → Zustand Store → ReactFlow Re-render
```

## BaseNode Interface

Every node must implement this exact interface:

```typescript
interface BaseNode {
  // Instance properties
  id: string;                    // unique node instance ID
  type: string;                  // node type slug
  version: number;               // schema version
  displayName: string;           // human readable name
  config: Record<string, any>;   // node configuration data
  meta: Record<string, any>;     // UI state (position, collapsed, etc)
  inputs: PortDefinition[];      // input port definitions
  outputs: PortDefinition[];     // output port definitions
  
  // Required methods
  getConfigSchema(): JsonSchemaObject;
  validateConfig(config: any): ValidationResult;
  serialize(): NodeSerializable;
  deserialize(snapshot: NodeSerializable): void;
  
  // Optional lifecycle hooks
  onAttach?(): void;
  onDetach?(): void;
  migrate?(oldConfig: any, oldVersion: number): any;
}

// Node definition interface for type metadata
interface NodeDefinition {
  type: string;                  // matches manifest.type
  version: number;               // matches manifest.version
  manifest: NodeManifest;        // the manifest.json content
}
```

## Node Folder Structure

Each node must follow this exact structure:

```
/src/nodes/<NodeName>/
├── manifest.json    # Node definition and schema
├── index.ts         # Exports manifest, Node, and NodeEditor
├── Node.ts          # BaseNode implementation (class or factory)
└── ui.tsx           # React editor component
```

